      "writtenOn": "2022-06-08T14:37:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think for code blocks that don\u0027t have children, we may as well keep it as AddBlock(). Many shaders don\u0027t have children and it is cumbersome to have to remember to call endBlock() right away. Related to that, maybe it\u0027s worth having a variant API on SkPaintParamsKeyBuilder that corresponds to adding a leaf block with a fixed number of bytes, so that even inside these functions we don\u0027t have the repeated lines of code of beginBlock(...); endBlock();",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 35,
        "startChar": 9,
        "endLine": 35,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "2f0ed6caac0aef37eeeb45dbfe6b3c6524eab013",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
